  "guards": [
    "Do not import or invent the initial attack/incident reporting deadlines: clause 5 points to a separate FSB procedure and states no number.",
    "The clause 6 24-hour identifier clock expressly starts when information is received in the personal account; Order 548 does not state an equivalent trigger for reserve-channel receipt.",
    "Clause 6 treats the identifier as confirmation of transfer; it must not be represented as a conclusion that the incident is resolved or the report is substantively complete.",
    "Reserve postal/email channels apply only upon technical failure and/or absence of communication with the personal account and use addresses recorded in that account.",
    "Clause 7 creates a right to request assistance, not a mandatory request for every incident.",
    "Clause 9 applies only to relevant threat information received from NCCCI and requires information about preventive measures, not proof that prevention succeeded.",
    "Under clause 10, requested information or a compliant inability notice is due within 24 hours; naming a later delivery time does not postpone the initial response deadline.",
    "Do not assign arbitrary numerical durations to the sequencing rule in clause 4 or the functions listed in clause 8."
  ]
